{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form","id":1465147,"title":"Death while in hishu form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-24T09:15:36-07:00","id":1465147,"title":"Death while in hishu form","content":"I've recently played a chronicle of WtF and saw an argument between the ST and a player regarding the way a wolf in hishu form could potentially be killed, during the game the player was took by surprise while investigating an appartment and took a 12 gauge into the back of his head, taking enough lethal damage to fill all the health box and actually get a point of aggravated, the storyteller deemed this an instant death but the player argued that, as a werewolf, he should be allowed to shift into garou form to regenerate. This actually got me curious, would a werewolf in hishu form be considered a human even for the purpose of determining damage and eventual death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T09:52:28-07:00","id":1465150,"title":"","content":"Rules as written, a track full of lethal damage isn't an instant death, even for an ordinary human. It does mean unconsciousness and beginning to bleed out (which inflicts an extra point of damage by the minute) unless arrested by emergency medical care, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition, p. 169</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf in Gauru form does not suffer wound penalties or need to roll to remain conscious, nor does he bleed out. In other forms, werewolves take damage as humans do, though they have incredible regenerative powers (\u201cRegeneration,\u201d p. 93).</div> </div> </div> </div>So taking this hit in any form but Gauru takes you down, and either you bleed out faster than your regeneration can keep up or your assailant finishes the job with a double-tap.<br /> <br /> Unless the werewolf was very high Harmony or out of Essence, he's likely able to shift into Gauru reflexively. The sticking point is: can you take a reflexive shapeshifting action *mid-taking damage?*<br /> <br /> I don't believe this is directly addressed in the books. In the case of ambush attacks, I'd be inclined to say no. By the time you're registering what's happening enough to shift, you've already taken the injury, and the injury is enough to down you. An unconscious wolf can't shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:30:22-07:00","id":1465159,"title":"","content":"Yeah, by RAW I'd say most of the ST reasoning is right, the caveat being that unless the killer take the time and effort to finish the job, which isn't necessarily likely, depends on the situation, a Uratha would actually survive and regenerate from this no problem, getting up in 15 minutes.<br /> <br /> But adding this caveat to the general circumstance, I'd say it was a dick move and ST and player must talk it out OoC. Both may or may not have been unreasonable, for many different reasons, not necessarily out of malice. So this isn't only a rules dilemma. It isn't ever just rules when a character dies and it doesn't feel right for everyone at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:09:54-07:00","id":1465187,"title":"","content":"The storyteller reasoning was that, rules aside, taking a point blank shot to the back of your head would basically blew the top part of your skull off and he said that a werewolf in hishu form, which is basically a human with sharper senses and a bit of regenerative power, could not come back from that. The player argued that werewolves are supposed to have the best regeneration of the whole CoD and even in human form, he should have just jumped up in garou form and heal everything minus the aggravated. We basically spent the rest of the session looking on the books and we really couldn't find nothing that would favor one part or the other, the core book in particular was very confusing and didn't bring answers to our problem. As far as this being a dick move, I won't annoy you with the kind of drama that comes with hoteaded players but if you gamed long enough you probably know exactly what I'm talking about and lets leave it at that. One thing thats really not clear on the core book is the regeneration of lethal wounds, the book states that &quot;Uratha heal their regeneration rate in of lethal damage every 15 minutes. By spending a point of Essence as a reflexive action, she may regenerate lethal damage instead of bashing damage for the turn.&quot;, what does it mean with their regeneration rate? does it mean that they heal all damage every 15 minutes like in garou form? also, can they spend essence while they are unconscious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:20:44-07:00","id":1465191,"title":"","content":"The books are all pretty clear on full Lethal and one Aggravated not killing you outright and Stupid Loserman quoted the section on bleeding out and unconsciousness.<br /> <br /> The justification is solely on the STs side. You can describe a head caving in and instantly killing someone with 1 Bashing damage. But if the mechanical damage done doesn't kill the target they shouldn't describe it as doing so any more than you would with 1 Bashing.<br /> <br /> Using the one Essence to upgrade healing changes it to your Primal Urge determined Bashing regenerated per turn. You can't upgrade while unconscious but they can't bleed out so would be considered stabilized and just have to wait.<br /> <br /> Gifts and fetishes can change everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:33:07-07:00","id":1465195,"title":"","content":"So he shouldn't have died from that at least from the numbers alone, could an uratha shapeshift to garou or even spend essence while in those conditions? this is probably the point I'm most conflicted about because on one end it makes sense that a wolf in hishu form could die from something like a shotgun blast to the head, its the human form afterall but on the other it would mean that all you would need to do to kill an uratha is to wait them at home after work and double tap them to the back of the head, I know about the wolf senses and such but those aren't infallible. I understand that it wouldn't be conceptually too different from finding a vampire haven and burning it in the morning and its a good reminder of ones mortality, memento mori and all but it still feels like, I don't know, anticlimatic. The reason I'm asking this is because I'm planning a campaign where humans would face most splats, including werewolves and wanted to know about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:38:58-07:00","id":1465197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465191#post1465191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Using the one Essence to upgrade healing changes it to your Primal Urge determined Bashing regenerated per turn. You can't upgrade while unconscious but they can't bleed out so would be considered stabilized and just have to wait.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where does it says that an uratha in hishu can't bleed out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:43:05-07:00","id":1465209,"title":"","content":"A 12 to the head should be guaranteed death to most people. Yet, people IRL have survived to all sorts of crazy stuff, including a 12 to the head. It is even more so if you consider that most lethal wounds don't actually kill you instantly no matter how grievous they are. And finally, the gunner targeting the head and the shot hitting it so perfectly are two different things.<br /> <br /> Your ST decided for the ambush. Your ST decided for a headshot. Your ST decided to describe it as hitting well enough. Your ST decided to let the description take precedence. Your ST decided that their dick move deserves ignoring the rules but the PC's survival don't.<br /> <br /> What killed this character was not the rules, the dice or the gunner, was the ST. Alone and unaided, fiat murder by deus ex machina.<br /> <br /> 1- You should describe the wound always based on the results on the dice. If the dice say full lethal plus 1 agg, describe accordingly;<br /> <br /> 2- Essence and Change can't be used reflexively if you're unconscious. Are you able to do so in response to the cause of loss of consciousness? Up to the ST to decide in a case by case basis, preferably with a good story in mind instead of being a dick;<br /> <br /> 3- Uratha regenerate lethal every 15 minutes regardless of form. Although it isn't directly stated, it is quick enough to regenerate the last point and stop any bleeding. In fact the bleeding should stop almost instantly since it is how even common human regeneration begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:06:56-07:00","id":1465213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465209#post1465209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ST decided for the ambush. Your ST decided for a headshot. Your ST decided to describe it as hitting well enough. Your ST decided to let the description take precedence. Your ST decided that their dick move deserves ignoring the rules but the PC's survival don't.<br /> <br /> What killed this character was not the rules, the dice or the gunner, was the ST. Alone and unaided, fiat murder by deus ex machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, given what details <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a> has reveled through this thread, I agree with both your thought process and conclusion. However neither one of us we're there and only have a single point of view on the matter.<br /> I'm just advocating on behalf of the devil.<br /> <br /> I understand the ST inclination to have a shotgun insta-kill an unaware victim, hell I've done it. Although not to a PC that seems deeply unsporting. Ideally there should be foreshadowing, clues and rolls to indicate an ambush and i don't think we should assume there wasn't.<br /> <br /> That all being said from my reading if you're rolled over into lethal and unconscious you start to bleed out at a rate of one point/health box per minute. in theory you would regenerate your right most lethal wound on your health track in 15 minutes, but unless you have more than 15 health boxes your going to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:52:20-07:00","id":1465222,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar252_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"252\" data-vbnamecard=\"252\">basketcase</a>, I don't know if the ST's dick move was motivated by a history of Player's dick moves or any other context indeed. But my answer is to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27142\" data-vbnamecard=\"27142\">Newb95</a>, who can take it and contextualize as they need to.<br /> <br /> The main point is that it was a bad move regardless, but it can be used to understand why it was bad and how it can be improved.<br /> <br /> Is there a personal conflict among players? Trying to solve it that way will only worse things. Is it the result of the ST rolling their vision of how the game should be? We must learn to temper our expectations for the sake of collective fun. Is really due to a conflict between the dice and the scene? Learning to weave the dice in the scene is a process.<br /> <br /> So while I am upset, I'm not posting that just to be judgemental, but to give and if possible get more data.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:01:29-07:00","id":1465224,"title":"","content":"The story teller gave plenty of foreshadowing, the shooter was the last survivor of a group of hunters the pack fought, the most experienced and the one who managed to elude the pack the longest, the player character, a rahoun called one of his contacts and got a possible location. Instead of being smart and informing the rest of the pack, the player decided, for no good reason, to play hero and went into the apartment alone, the idiot didn't even shift dalu and just came barging into the apartment, dice rolled and the hunter won. Story aside, the player and the st had beef (it was that kind of game unfortunately) and while this was a blatant attempt on the st to get rid of him, it also got me thinking that this would be the most logical outcome given the circumstances, even if the st didn't cheat and straight up murdered the player, the latter would still most likely end up dead because if an uratha is unconscious and can't spend essence to upgrade his healing to lethal, he would also die before the 15 minutes had passed. What I wanted to know was if an uratha could shift while unconscious but from what I gather, its largely up to the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:17:27-07:00","id":1465227,"title":"","content":"It's largely up to the ST and the PC would die anyway because if that was a hunter the gunner wouldn't let the job to the bleeding. But you see, by cheating the player the ST made it into another unnecessary issue for no reason. They should solve it out of game or just stop playing together if it is that bad, and I wish you good luck with your upcoming humans game.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, upon the death of a PC the player should feel closure. This is tricky, but easier done than said, actually. If the player feel cheated or victimized, no rule will cover this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:35:14-07:00","id":1465229,"title":"","content":"The game already died, I also thought that the storyteller messed up but I guess he was at his breaking point with the guy, some people just don't get along and ruin it for everyone. Anyway thanks for the answers, I guess that the go to method to deal with an uratha is to catch them when in hishu, make sense otherwise they would be too op but I can work something out for my campaign, looking for a giant monstrosity is not easy when you are hunted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-24-2021, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:34:27-07:00","id":1465249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form#post1465147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently played a chronicle of WtF and saw an argument between the ST and a player regarding the way a wolf in hishu form could potentially be killed, during the game the player was took by surprise while investigating an appartment and took a 12 gauge into the back of his head, taking enough lethal damage to fill all the health box and actually get a point of aggravated, the storyteller deemed this an instant death but the player argued that, as a werewolf, he should be allowed to shift into garou form to regenerate. This actually got me curious, would a werewolf in hishu form be considered a human even for the purpose of determining damage and eventual death?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST has it wrong as long as the Uratha has Essence to spend. Spending Essence is a reflexive action for a werewolf and can even be done while bleeding out. The moment the character went down with full lethal and that hit of aggravated, they spent a point of Essence to kickstart their healing. The next turn, they healed at least one lethal level, stopped bleeding out, woke up and could even act if they wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:36:07-07:00","id":1465250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465249#post1465249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST has it wrong as long as the Uratha has Essence to spend. Spending Essence is a reflexive action for a werewolf and can even be done while bleeding out. The moment the character went down with full lethal and that hit of aggravated, they spent a point of Essence to kickstart their healing. The next turn, they healed at least one lethal level, stopped bleeding out, woke up and could even act if they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they fall unconscious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:46:15-07:00","id":1465251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465187#post1465187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The storyteller reasoning was that, rules aside, taking a point blank shot to the back of your head would basically blew the top part of your skull off and he said that a werewolf in hishu form, which is basically a human with sharper senses and a bit of regenerative power, could not come back from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>First up, the ST can rule as they please for their game, and if that\u2019s the way they want to play it, sure.<br /> <br /> But, if we\u2019re going by what Uratha are and the rules for them, no. A Uratha in hishu is in no way \u201cbasically a human with sharper senses\u201d. It\u2019s a werewolf that happens to be wearing its human-form disguise at the moment. Werewolf first and always, the form that it happens to be in doesn\u2019t take that away.<br /> <br /> Werewolf regeneration isn\u2019t pretty, either. Blow the back of a Uratha\u2019s head off with a shotgun and it\u2019ll fall to the ground. Then, when its Essence healing kicks in, tendrils of blood and brain will reach out to each other. Disgusting slurping sounds happen. The gore pulls fragments of skull back together and then drags them back to what\u2019s left of the head. Weird grinding sounds occur as jagged bone bits adjust themselves like a self-assembling jigsaw, trying to work out how they fit back together. And when most of it\u2019s done, flesh and bone start growing into the gaps, leaving some splatter on the ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The player argued that werewolves are supposed to have the best regeneration of the whole CoD and even in human form, he should have just jumped up in garou form and heal everything minus the aggravated. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing thats really not clear on the core book is the regeneration of lethal wounds, the book states that &amp;quot;Uratha heal their regeneration rate in of lethal damage every 15 minutes. By spending a point of Essence as a reflexive action, she may regenerate lethal damage instead of bashing damage for the turn.&amp;quot;, what does it mean with their regeneration rate? does it mean that they heal all damage every 15 minutes like in garou form? also, can they spend essence while they are unconscious? </div> </div> </div>Uratha heal a certain amount of bashing damage each turn based on the Primal Urge trait. If they spend Essence they instead regenerate this amount of lethal damage in the turn. If they just find somewhere to hide and lay low, they still regenerate bashing each turn, and every 15 minutes they regenerate 1 level of lethal damage without having to spend Essence.<br /> <br /> You can run a Uratha down with a truck, back up over the pieces a few times, but leave them lying in the gutter for a few hours and they\u2019ll be back up like nothing happened. (Well, not quite like nothing happened. You now have a pissed off werewolf looking to hunt you down for payback.)<br /> <br /> Answering that last point - can they spend Essence while unconscious? For reflexive things like healing, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:49:18-07:00","id":1465252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465250#post1465250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if they fall unconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Let me expand on this further. The character isn\u2019t (shouldn\u2019t be) unconscious when they choose to spend Essence. Spending Essence on regeneration is reflexive, which can be done at any time. With injury, if the track fills with bashing you roll Stamina to remain conscious. Nothing requires the character to wait until the outcome of that roll to overcharge their regeneration. Being unconscious from massive damage is a bad state for a Uratha to be in, so the character reflexively spends the Essence before (possibly) failing the Stamina roll and falling unconscious. Then they regenerate at least one lethal box and wake up. <br /> <br /> Or, if they want, they spend that Essence point to reflexively shift to Gauru before the Stamina roll. They regenerate all lethal and no longer have to even bother with the Stamina roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T02:38:17-07:00","id":1465257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465252#post1465252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Let me expand on this further. The character isn\u2019t (shouldn\u2019t be) unconscious when they choose to spend Essence. Spending Essence on regeneration is reflexive, which can be done at any time. With injury, if the track fills with bashing you roll Stamina to remain conscious. Nothing requires the character to wait until the outcome of that roll to overcharge their regeneration. Being unconscious from massive damage is a bad state for a Uratha to be in, so the character reflexively spends the Essence before (possibly) failing the Stamina roll and falling unconscious. Then they regenerate at least one lethal box and wake up.<br /> <br /> Or, if they want, they spend that Essence point to reflexively shift to Gauru before the Stamina roll. They regenerate all lethal and no longer have to even bother with the Stamina roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm even more confused now, other people here have said that you can't use essence while unconscious, now you are saying that they can before rolling their unconscious roll which would defeat the purpose of an unconscious roll in the first place, same goes for turning garou, which would require a turn or another point of essence (harmony not withstanding). Again the books aren't clear on this, if the uratha in hishu can spend essence point before rolling for unconsciousness it would basically mean that they wouldn't even fall to the ground before starting to regenerate, that looks more like a zombie to me, and frankly, if the writers intentions were this from the start they should have wrote it cleanly on the book, something along the line &quot;uratha don't have to roll unconscious because they can spend essence to regenerate lethal&quot;. Again, I'm even more confused now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:05:56-07:00","id":1465264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465257#post1465257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm even more confused now, other people here have said that you can't use essence while unconscious, now you are saying that they can before rolling their unconscious roll</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which would defeat the purpose of an unconscious roll in the first place </div> </div> </div>No, you need Essence to spend to avoid it, and make the choice to spend the Essence, neither of which are guaranteed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it would basically mean that they wouldn't even fall to the ground before starting to regenerate </div> </div> </div>And? Uratha regeneration is aggressively efficient, much like the Uratha.<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolf regeneration is not a peaceful healing process. Uratha regeneration is the body\u2019s stark defiance against anything that would destroy it. It\u2019s the wolf\u2019s wild instincts to survive, taken to a rapid and violent extreme. For anything but a superficial wound, regeneration looks unnatural and perverted to the average person. Muscles grind and twist to return to where they need to be. Bones fuse with a faint hiss as cells split apart and grab one another eagerly. Torn skin whips around until it finds its match across the wound.&quot; - W:TF 2e p.93.<br /> <br /> Uratha regeneration doesn't look subtle, nice, or non-supernatural. It causes Lunacy in onlookers!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , that looks more like a zombie to me </div> </div> </div>That's a weird take on this, but if that's how you see it, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , and frankly, if the writers intentions were this from the start they should have wrote it cleanly on the book </div> </div> </div>Your faith in us is admirable but we're human. We thought it was clear - that often happens when you understand what you're trying to say and don't see that others may not get it. Hindsight is 20/20, as they say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I'm even more confused now. </div> </div> </div>Here's the simple version:<br /> 1. The ST was wrong by the rules.<br /> 2. The player was right by the rules.<br /> 3. However, most importantly, and something that we on the forums aren't going to every change, the ST can use or change rules at their table and run it how they want. In which case, the ST's decision/interpretation is correct because of this.<br /> <br /> If you're going with 1 and 2, the moral of the story is that if you want to take on Uratha, you force them to drain their Essence, you bring sources of aggravated damage, and you hit them harder than what you think. Overkill isn't too much if you're wanting to survive against the apex predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-25-2021, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:15:53-07:00","id":1465266,"title":"","content":"Wait, you are one of the writers of the 2nd edition? if thats the case I'll take your words for it, this puts me in a bad spot for my campaign though, I want to be as faithfull to the rules as possible and I need a way for a group of normal people to kill a werewolf (not the only possible approach but I need the option) and since they are basically unkillable in any of the other forms, I really don't know how to work around this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:19:40-07:00","id":1465267,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re not unkillable, it just takes more than a shotgun to the back if the head that only does 1 aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:37:01-07:00","id":1465270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465267#post1465267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re not unkillable, it just takes more than a shotgun to the back if the head that only does 1 aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>My campaign won't have a phased rifle in the 40 watt range, I will think of something, if anything I will pick another antagonist, werewolves are too much for other supernaturals let alone humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T06:35:35-07:00","id":1465271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465270#post1465270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My campaign won't have a phased rifle in the 40 watt range, I will think of something, if anything I will pick another antagonist, werewolves are too much for other supernaturals let alone humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of God aside, it won't get easier if you don't want to change the rules, but it isn't as impossible as you seem to think.<br /> <br /> You're giving too much credit to a character that tried to off a werewolf just by sneaking alone with a shotgun. This is a loosing strategy for a hunter. A human vs splat fight isn't just hard, it is a human vs a monster. The human must compensate with teamwork, cunning and liberal exploration of the target's weaknesses.<br /> <br /> If that shotgun had silver, even with reduced damage, everything would be aggravated. Even if the werewolf survived the encounter the wound would take too much time to heal. If the gunner had a good enough position to run and get a second shot, silver maybe would not be necessary. If there were three gunners, the fight would end up similarly.<br /> <br /> From the hunter perspective it was a desperate, hopeless tactic, and yet was a close call. You want to compare it to a vampire? Instead of a single aggravated you would have a single lethal in the track and a pissed off predator healing with blood and seeing you as a box of juice to replenish the batteries. A Mage would solve the problem without going in to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just let your players know that it isn't just a hard fight, it is a deathtrap, no matter the splat, it is to go against the very monsters of horror stories.<br /> <br /> And you'll have plenty to work with for lesser opponents. If the human PCs are facing splats, they should interact much more with lesser cousins anyways. Werewolves are rarer than Wolf Blooded, and yet the later are already terrifying monsters for common people. Many encounters with&quot;werewolves&quot; are actually with them. But they're far more killable if push comes to shove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T06:56:34-07:00","id":1465272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465271#post1465271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word of God aside, it won't get easier if you don't want to change the rules, but it isn't as impossible as you seem to think.<br /> <br /> You're giving too much credit to a character that tried to off a werewolf just by sneaking alone with a shotgun. This is a loosing strategy for a hunter. A human vs splat fight isn't just hard, it is a human vs a monster. The human must compensate with teamwork, cunning and liberal exploration of the target's weaknesses.<br /> <br /> If that shotgun had silver, even with reduced damage, everything would be aggravated. Even if the werewolf survived the encounter the wound would take too much time to heal. If the gunner had a good enough position to run and get a second shot, silver maybe would not be necessary. If there were three gunners, the fight would end up similarly.<br /> <br /> From the hunter perspective it was a desperate, hopeless tactic, and yet was a close call. You want to compare it to a vampire? Instead of a single aggravated you would have a single lethal in the track and a pissed off predator healing with blood and seeing you as a box of juice to replenish the batteries. A Mage would solve the problem without going in to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just let your players know that it isn't just a hard fight, it is a deathtrap, no matter the splat, it is to go against the very monsters of horror stories.<br /> <br /> And you'll have plenty to work with for lesser opponents. If the human PCs are facing splats, they should interact much more with lesser cousins anyways. Werewolves are rarer than Wolf Blooded, and yet the later are already terrifying monsters for common people. Many encounters with&quot;werewolves&quot; are actually with them. But they're far more killable if push comes to shove.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does silver work even in hishu form? I thought it only worked in the other forms, if thats the case, then it would make it more feasible. The campaign is basically about a ghost wolf, irraka serial killer, I made him following standard character creation so he doesn't have any crazy gifts bar his standards moon gifts and the garble facet (the one that lets you mess with electronics), one of the many ways to deal with him (and the one I would push the character toward) is to get in contact with an uratha pack and enlist their help to fix the problem but since it might not be possible (we are talking about extended social battles here) I wanted to leave the door open for characters to deal with him personally, I would be very clear that its borderline suicidal but I want it to be an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:18:38-07:00","id":1465273,"title":"","content":"Don't worry too much. If a single shot to the head with a perfectly legal and common gun, even if gruesome, were enough, it wouldn't be borderline suicidal, it would be slightly harder murder. You'll have an entire group of players able to come up with solutions for the problem and you'll have the more amenable Uratha as a means to show them just how hard it is before the final confrontation.<br /> <br /> Have your players watch them recovering from something with ease and let the PCs do the rest. Don't be afraid of selling the danger as even greater than it actually is. And don't expect them to just outsmart the villain, let them outsmart <b><u>you</u></b>. If they can't, make them have someone with an invested interest in saving their asses, so you can get them out of trouble once or twice &quot;without&quot; deus ex machina.<br /> <br /> I can't confirm by now if silver works in Hishu, but I think so since the regeneration does. One thing I want to know, though. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>, does the Uratha still bleed to death, 1dmg per minute, if they have to rely only on passive regeneration for whatever reason? Because this is one I really think shouldn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Emphasis 10-25-2021, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:32:43-07:00","id":1465275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465273#post1465273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry too much. If a single shot to the head with a perfectly legal and common gun, even if gruesome, were enough, it wouldn't be borderline suicidal, it would be slightly harder murder. You'll have an entire group of players able to come up with solutions for the problem and you'll have the more amenable Uratha as a means to show them just how hard it is before the final confrontation.<br /> <br /> Have your players watch them recovering from something with ease and let the PCs do the rest. Don't be afraid of selling the danger as even greater than it actually is. And don't expect them to just outsmart the villain, let them outsmart you. If they can't, make them have someone with an invested interest in saving their asses, so you can get them out of trouble once or twice &quot;without&quot; deus ex machina.<br /> <br /> I can't confirm by now if silver works in Hishu, but I think so since the regeneration does. One thing I want to know, though. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>, does the Uratha still bleed to death, 1dmg per minute, if they have to rely only on passive regeneration for whatever reason? Because this is one I really think shouldn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the tips, it will be the first game as a story teller and I'm a bit nervous about everything, I checked and from what I read on the manual, there is nothing that says that silver is not aggravated to hishu, the human form not being affected by silver was a garou (apocalypse) thing. This makes my idea for an ambush more viable since a skilled shooter with a shotgun loaded with silver (they actually sell it on the internet) would actually work (another mistake from the story teller in the campaign I played, the hunter could have used silver buckshot and it would all have been within the rules). I'm also interested in the bleeding out question, say a werewolf runs out of essence and can't either shift to garou or upgrade the damage regen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T07:46:42-07:00","id":1465277,"title":"","content":"I figured out it could be your first time, hence most of my rantings.<br /> <br /> The last advice is to not be too hard on yourself with applying the rules. You'll have some hiccups, that's inevitable. Let the fun of the game talk louder than rules. Most of the gist of it you'll get with actual experience, there's no way around it, but it's on you to have the learning process be fun or not. Choose fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:00:10-07:00","id":1465279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465277#post1465277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured out it could be your first time, hence most of my rantings.<br /> <br /> The last advice is to not be too hard on yourself with applying the rules. You'll have some hiccups, that's inevitable. Let the fun of the game talk louder than rules. Most of the gist of it you'll get with actual experience, there's no way around it, but it's on you to have the learning process be fun or not. Choose fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think I will be bending the rules a bit, it wouldn't be fun to lose a player at the first session because of a failed roll, I will still keep the werewolf lethal and basicaly impossible to take head on but I will be applying some bonuses to the lunacy checks and make them progressively easier until removing them altogether, I want to think of the players as the main character of a movie so a bit of plot armor here and there won't hurt the fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:39:49-07:00","id":1465283,"title":"","content":"You don't need to think ahead of time how you'll bend the rules. As I said you'll have hiccups, so preparation wise keep it simple, don't houserule. Instead, be prepared to not be too strict on yourself during game. You'll forget rules. You'll confuse rules. You'll have issues here and there. That's when you just go with gut feeling and rehearse things later.<br /> <br /> Managing rules as an ST is a very different beast from learning them as player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T08:59:33-07:00","id":1465285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465283#post1465283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to think ahead of time how you'll bend the rules. As I said you'll have hiccups, so preparation wise keep it simple, don't houserule. Instead, be prepared to not be too strict on yourself during game. You'll forget rules. You'll confuse rules. You'll have issues here and there. That's when you just go with gut feeling and rehearse things later.<br /> <br /> Managing rules as an ST is a very different beast from learning them as player.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks again for the tips, I guess I know everything I need for my campaign, time to get to the drawing board and work the details then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T09:57:00-07:00","id":1465288,"title":"","content":"I ve a doubt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> ,<br /> Given the high amount of damage to the head, it s correct to assume that the werewolf would be Stunned for a turn?<br /> Does the Stunned tilt prevents him to make even reflexive actions, like spending essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:19:21-07:00","id":1465291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465288#post1465288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ve a doubt <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> ,<br /> Given the high amount of damage to the head, it s correct to assume that the werewolf would be Stunned for a turn?<br /> Does the Stunned tilt prevents him to make even reflexive actions, like spending essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Stunned Tilt (which absolutely does apply in this situation) specifically only prohibits Instant Actions (unless you spend WP to end the Tilt and just take a penalty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:36:21-07:00","id":1465294,"title":"","content":"To me the 'to the head' part just seems like another aspect of the ST's flourish rather than any specific attempt to aim.<br /> <br /> And yes, silver is impactful against werewolves in all forms providing it's of pure enough grade. That said it's also a universal trigger so a werewolf hit with it will be automatically shifting towards gauru soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2021, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:41:22-07:00","id":1465295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465187#post1465187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The storyteller reasoning was that, rules aside, taking a point blank shot to the back of your head would basically blew the top part of your skull off</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Storyteller has seen too many movies.<br /> <br /> Besides, I should think the whole point of rolling dice is that you make the action emerge from the result. If it was not sufficient to fill the health track with aggravated damage, then it shouldn't be taking the form of the most grievous injury possible. Point blank but badly angled, or a quirk in the spread of the buckshot, or whatever else is needed to leave an injury severe but within the possibility to survive with emergency medical attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:56:33-07:00","id":1465298,"title":"","content":"The storyteller didn't make it a called shot, he just rolled and killed the guy, it wasn't a mishap in the rules but a blatant attempt to get rid of the player, I guess he had reached his limit with the guy since he forgot to use silver but yeah the whole episode was the culmination of a long string of out of character fighting between the two, personally I don't care because as far as I'm concerned they were both two assholes who ruined it for everyone so it is what it is. Anyway its clear that 80% silver will get the job done even in hishu form and that was everything I needed to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:06:21-07:00","id":1465300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465294#post1465294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, silver is impactful against werewolves in all forms providing it's of pure enough grade. That said it's also a universal trigger so a werewolf hit with it will be automatically shifting towards gauru soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soon wouldn't be enough, he got enough Lethal to roll out from clean to Agg. Of course, I personally think using silver would reduce the Damage Rating, can't look at the books to see if this is RAW right now, but they would need a -2 to damage for the victim to live enough to Change.<br /> <br /> At the very least it would be far more uncertain if the character would be able or not to spend Essence and Change, making it look a little less dickish, and even if they lived it would be simpler to just have someone run over the Gauru with a truck and finish the job abiding to the rules.<br /> <br /> Would I do it that way? No, I would've ruled in favor of the PC living if I had any doubt. But then, no player of mine complains that I'm a dick and I've already rooted out the dick players from my main group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:25:29-07:00","id":1465304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465300#post1465300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soon wouldn't be enough, he got enough Lethal to roll out from clean to Agg. Of course, I personally think using silver would reduce the Damage Rating, can't look at the books to see if this is RAW right now, but they would need a -2 to damage for the victim to live enough to Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you think so. The same situation happened to me, except it was a spirit with Blast. And I used the unclear qualifier 'soon' because if the werewolf has a good Harmony they could just switch to gauru that turn. If not they would at least be shifting one form over, getting the extra Health and now not being surprised, instead being capable of just disabling the gun with a Gift or killing the attacker some other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the very least it would be far more uncertain if the character would be able or not to spend Essence and Change, making it look a little less dickish, and even if they lived it would be simpler to just have someone run over the Gauru with a truck and finish the job abiding to the rules.<br /> <br /> Would I do it that way? No, I would've ruled in favor of the PC living if I had any doubt. But then, no player of mine complains that I'm a dick and I've already rooted out the dick players from my main group. </div> </div> </div>I mean, you're already having a werewolf not notice someone hiding behind a door in their own apartment. If you want to add a truck hiding in their closet waiting to run them over that should stretch suspension of disbelief well past the breaking point. I'm not sure where 'You lose your werewolf abilities' would make it 'a little less dickish.' This seems to be a regular gun not some sort of template-removal ray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:29:34-07:00","id":1465305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465300#post1465300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soon wouldn't be enough, he got enough Lethal to roll out from clean to Agg. Of course, I personally think using silver would reduce the Damage Rating, can't look at the books to see if this is RAW right now, but they would need a -2 to damage for the victim to live enough to Change.<br /> <br /> At the very least it would be far more uncertain if the character would be able or not to spend Essence and Change, making it look a little less dickish, and even if they lived it would be simpler to just have someone run over the Gauru with a truck and finish the job abiding to the rules.<br /> <br /> Would I do it that way? No, I would've ruled in favor of the PC living if I had any doubt. But then, no player of mine complains that I'm a dick and I've already rooted out the dick players from my main group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't read anywhere that silver weapons do -2 damage (I know that improvised only work once as a damage source) but If you want to houserule it for your uratha players that would avoid untimely deaths and keep the fun going, In my human campaign werewolves are plenty dangerous already, so if one of the players can manage to research about werewolves weaknesses (the hard part), get a shotgun and reload some shells with silver pellets (the easy part, even in real life shotgun shells can be loaded with practically anything that fits in) and finaly nail a werewolf with a shot (the absurdly difficult part) then the pooch will feel all the silver he gets.<br /> As far as dick players and story tellers, this two morons were the exceptions, most of the players I met were cool and the st fair, it ain't going to ruin werewolf for me thats for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:31:10-07:00","id":1465306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465291#post1465291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Stunned Tilt (which absolutely does apply in this situation) specifically only prohibits Instant Actions (unless you spend WP to end the Tilt and just take a penalty).</div> </div> </div> </div>From which core book are you looking for the tilt?<br /> All the versions i ve checked only states an ambiguous &quot;you lose your next action&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:44:37-07:00","id":1465308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465304#post1465304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure why you think so. The same situation happened to me, except it was a spirit with Blast. And I used the unclear qualifier 'soon' because if the werewolf has a good Harmony they could just switch to gauru that turn. If not they would at least be shifting one form over, getting the extra Health and now not being surprised, instead being capable of just disabling the gun with a Gift or killing the attacker some other way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, you're already having a werewolf not notice someone hiding behind a door in their own apartment. If you want to add a car hiding in their closet waiting to run them over that should stretch suspension of disbelief well past the breaking point. I'm not sure where 'You lose your werewolf abilities' would make it 'a little less dickish.' This seems to be a regular gun not some sort of template-removal ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much of a dick the st was, I can't say he didn't give the player plenty of chances to think about it, as I wrote before the player acted like an idiot, before the st triggered the death trap he gave the player the chance to roll 3 times which he failed fair and square, so the player is not innocent in all of this, the dick move wasn't the ambush but the fact that he decided to overule the rules and just straight up kill the player.<br /> As far as the uratha shifting to garou when full of aggravated, thats kinda of a stretch in my opinion, the rules for damage say that you die when all the health box fill with aggravated, stop, no reflexive actions or other saves, you just die, If Bunyip says otherwise than thats word of god but again, if one of my players had the skill/luck to ambush an uratha with silver and then deal enough aggravated then he deserves the kill, a different case would be a werewolf player were deus ex machina would come to the rescue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:45:27-07:00","id":1465309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465306#post1465306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From which core book are you looking for the tilt?<br /> All the versions i ve checked only states an ambiguous &quot;you lose your next action&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Action&quot; and &quot;Instant Action&quot; are interchangeable. It also says &quot;during her own action&quot; which can only mean during the character's turn when they're allowed to take an instant action.<br /> Also, since it only prevents a single action, if it also applied to reflexive actions you'd just be able to waste one of your unlimited reflexive actions and then just do whatever reflexive or instant action you intended to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:50:11-07:00","id":1465310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465308#post1465308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the uratha shifting to garou when full of aggravated, thats kinda of a stretch in my opinion, the rules for damage say that you die when all the health box fill with aggravated, stop, no reflexive actions or other saves, you just die,</div> </div> </div> </div>No one has said anything about full aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:02:56-07:00","id":1465313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465304#post1465304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure why you think so. The same situation happened to me, except it was a spirit with Blast. And I used the unclear qualifier 'soon' because if the werewolf has a good Harmony they could just switch to gauru that turn. If not they would at least be shifting one form over, getting the extra Health and now not being surprised, instead being capable of just disabling the gun with a Gift or killing the attacker some other way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, you're already having a werewolf not notice someone hiding behind a door in their own apartment. If you want to add a truck hiding in their closet waiting to run them over that should stretch suspension of disbelief well past the breaking point. I'm not sure where 'You lose your werewolf abilities' would make it 'a little less dickish.' This seems to be a regular gun not some sort of template-removal ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't the the player's appartment but a possible safehouse for an hunter, the st had the player roll 3 times which he failed fair and square, the dick move wasn't the ambush but the fact that he killed him like that. Anyway I think that what you are suggesting about shifting into garou when at full aggravated, is a bit of a stretch, the rules say that once you fill your last health box with aggravated you are dead, no reflexive action or other saves are allowed, if Bunyip says so then its world of god but otherwise that doesn't seem to be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:06:32-07:00","id":1465314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465310#post1465310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one has said anything about full aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was answering to nofather comment about shifting when full aggravated, I apologize if thats not what he meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:47:54-07:00","id":1465318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465313#post1465313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't the the player's appartment but a possible safehouse for an hunter, the st had the player roll 3 times which he failed fair and square, the dick move wasn't the ambush but the fact that he killed him like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway I think that what you are suggesting about shifting into garou when at full aggravated, is a bit of a stretch, the rules say that once you fill your last health box with aggravated you are dead, no reflexive action or other saves are allowed, if Bunyip says so then its world of god but otherwise that doesn't seem to be the case. </div> </div> </div>I agree with the ruling, but I'm not suggesting shifting when at full Aggravated (when you would be dead, beyond some abilities). I don't believe a similar roll would result in the same amount of successes outside of another 'rocks fall, you die' call. A different situation, like in your games, where you're trying to kill a hishu with a silver bullet can just as easily lead to them only taking 2 damage and then going swiftly to gauru.<br /> <br /> Though for simplicity's sake, in a game with human or hunter players, it's easier (for the ST and the PCs) to use Horrors that emulate werewolves rather than actual Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2021, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:56:55-07:00","id":1465319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465304#post1465304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about the same roll, if it were with silver. The gunner got enough on a normal shot to roll over to Agg. If it was silver, then it would've killed the target straight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465305#post1465305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read anywhere that silver weapons do -2 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not saying it did, just gave an example. As I said, I couldn't verify the books at the time. And I do make silver generally less damaging, I don't know in a shotgun, but I would compare with loading it with other shitty stuff, but this is mostly me, unless you want to delve into the threads in Apocalypse about silver as a weapon.<br /> <br /> Don't sweat it one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:05:59-07:00","id":1465321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465318#post1465318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with the ruling, but I'm not suggesting shifting when at full Aggravated (when you would be dead, beyond some abilities). I don't believe a similar roll would result in the same amount of successes outside of another 'rocks fall, you die' call. A different situation, like in your games, where you're trying to kill a hishu with a silver bullet can just as easily lead to them only taking 2 damage and then going swiftly to gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the dice gods give just as easily as they take but depending on the gun used, like a rifle that gives a +4 to damage means that at 3 successes you get 7 points of aggravated (with silver of course), thats enough to kill an hishu in an ambush and frankly its not even that difficult of a roll, a character with 3 dex and 3 guns plus 3 points of will power and using a scope (I think thats another plus 2 but I'm not sure) and you would be rolling 10 to 12 dices, so while its still possible to mess up, you would still have a good chance to pull it off, the hard thing would be to ambush an hishu and get past his wolf senses but there are ways for that, like a scent killer spray, I think I saw in the armory supplement but I might be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:06:36-07:00","id":1465322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465272#post1465272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does silver work even in hishu form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve missed a lot of this thread due to sleeping (time zones!) but on aquick skim didn\u2019t see that anyone had directly addressed this.<br /> <br /> Silver works in any form. Unlike Garou (Werewolf the Apocalypse), Uratha don\u2019t have a breed form that isn\u2019t vulnerable to silver. Uratha are werewolves in all their forms, all of which are as natural and comfortable as the others. <br /> <br /> Their auspice provides some protection, however. The silver has to be 80%+ pure, and it gas to be a weapon. They can touch silver cutlery or jewelry without damage. It may not be comfortable but it\u2019s not damaging. The Pure werewolves don\u2019t have this protection (having removed their auspices) - silver always burns them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:09:13-07:00","id":1465323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465318#post1465318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with the ruling, but I'm not suggesting shifting when at full Aggravated (when you would be dead, beyond some abilities). I don't believe a similar roll would result in the same amount of successes outside of another 'rocks fall, you die' call. A different situation, like in your games, where you're trying to kill a hishu with a silver bullet can just as easily lead to them only taking 2 damage and then going swiftly to gauru.<br /> <br /> Though for simplicity's sake, in a game with human or hunter players, it's easier (for the ST and the PCs) to use Horrors that emulate werewolves rather than actual Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course the dice gods give just as easily as they take but depending on the gun used, like a rifle that gives a +4 to damage means that at 3 successes you get 7 points of aggravated (with silver of course), thats enough to kill an hishu in an ambush and frankly its not even that difficult of a roll, a character with 3 dex and 3 guns plus 3 points of will power and using a scope (I think thats another plus 2 but I'm not sure) and you would be rolling 10 to 12 dices, so while its still possible to mess up, you would still have a good chance to pull it off, the hard thing would be to ambush an hishu and get past his wolf senses but there are ways for that, like a scent killer spray, I think I saw in the armory supplement but I might be wrong.<br /> About using horrors, I don't think that would change much, they are still very dangerous for a human and in my campaign I'm going to try and push my players toward a different solution than direct engagement anyway.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:15:45-07:00","id":1465324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465322#post1465322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve missed a lot of this thread due to sleeping (time zones!) but on aquick skim didn\u2019t see that anyone had directly addressed this.<br /> <br /> Silver works in any form. Unlike Garou (Werewolf the Apocalypse), Uratha don\u2019t have a breed form that isn\u2019t vulnerable to silver. Uratha are werewolves in all their forms, all of which are as natural and comfortable as the others.<br /> <br /> Their auspice provides some protection, however. The silver has to be 80%+ pure, and it gas to be a weapon. They can touch silver cutlery or jewelry without damage. It may not be comfortable but it\u2019s not damaging. The Pure werewolves don\u2019t have this protection (having removed their auspices) - silver always burns them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, my old st must have been fuming with rage since he could have just said that the shooter used silver buckshot and be done with it, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:25:14-07:00","id":1465325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465288#post1465288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ve a doubt <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> ,<br /> Given the high amount of damage to the head, it s correct to assume that the werewolf would be Stunned for a turn?<br /> Does the Stunned tilt prevents him to make even reflexive actions, like spending essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stunned is certainly appropriate for a werewolf having its head blown apart and needing to regenerate. But no, it doesn\u2019t prevent reflexive Essence expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:27:50-07:00","id":1465326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465294#post1465294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, silver is impactful against werewolves in all forms providing it's of pure enough grade. That said it's also a universal trigger so a werewolf hit with it will be automatically shifting towards gauru soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent point as well. If you\u2019re going to use silver on a werewolf, expect things to escalate, fast. Put them down in one shot because you may not get a second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:29:13-07:00","id":1465327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465298#post1465298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The storyteller didn't make it a called shot, he just rolled and killed the guy, it wasn't a mishap in the rules but a blatant attempt to get rid of the player, I guess he had reached his limit with the guy since he forgot to use silver but yeah the whole episode was the culmination of a long string of out of character fighting between the two, personally I don't care because as far as I'm concerned they were both two assholes who ruined it for everyone so it is what it is. Anyway its clear that 80% silver will get the job done even in hishu form and that was everything I needed to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I\u2019m happy we could help and sorry for our various rantings towards you. We werewolf fans tend to be a passionate lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:35:10-07:00","id":1465329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465305#post1465305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my human campaign werewolves are plenty dangerous already, so if one of the players can manage to research about werewolves weaknesses (the hard part), get a shotgun and reload some shells with silver pellets (the easy part, even in real life shotgun shells can be loaded with practically anything that fits in) and finaly nail a werewolf with a shot (the absurdly difficult part) then the pooch will feel all the silver he gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. My general approach is to lean in the protagonists\u2019 favor. In a werewolf game, the protagonists are Uratha and incredibly hard for nobodies to kill. But Uratha are designed to face threats bigger than nobodies.<br /> <br /> *But* if I\u2019m running a human game, werewolves are easier to kill. Their weaknesses are more profound. Something that the players discover and want to use will be more effective. If the example was a human game and the werewolf was an ST antagonist, a shotgun to the back of the head from one of the player\u2019s characters probably would have worked to put it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 10-25-2021, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:39:18-07:00","id":1465330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465314#post1465314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I was answering to nofather comment about shifting when full aggravated, I apologize if thats not what he meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t seen what you\u2019re replying to, but for clarity - if all your health boxes are marked with aggravated, you\u2019re dead. The only reflexive actions or abilities that might work are ones specifically designed to trigger when you\u2019re at death\u2019s door, and they\u2019d be specifically worded as such to make it clear. But I can\u2019t think of any of those in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T15:23:22-07:00","id":1465336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465327#post1465327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I\u2019m happy we could help and sorry for our various rantings towards you. We werewolf fans tend to be a passionate lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for helping me, I'm new to the forum and didn't know you were one of the writers, nothing like word of god to put doubts to rest<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. also no problem with rants or anything, all the people who replied the post were helpfull one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-25-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T15:25:23-07:00","id":1465337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465325#post1465325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stunned is certainly appropriate for a werewolf having its head blown apart and needing to regenerate. But no, it doesn\u2019t prevent reflexive Essence expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the werewolf in question would be able to spend essence to regenerate or shift directly into garou, would the shift happen in the same lost turn or the next? this could mean life and death for the shooter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T15:38:02-07:00","id":1465338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465329#post1465329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. My general approach is to lean in the protagonists\u2019 favor. In a werewolf game, the protagonists are Uratha and incredibly hard for nobodies to kill. But Uratha re designed to face threats bigger than nobidies.<br /> <br /> *But* if I\u2019m running a human game, werewolves are easier to kill. Their weaknesses are more profound. Something that the players discover and want to use will be more effective. If the example was a human game and the werewolf was an ST antagonist, a shotgun to the back of the head from one of the player\u2019s characters probably would have worked to put it down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will adopt a similar approach to my game, my werewolf Hannibal Lecter will be just as strong as a regular werewolf and the players will get no bonus to their damage rolls but lunacy will be nerfed a little. I will not put players into situations where they would suffer excessive ammounts of lethal damage (unless they really force my hand with stupid decisions) but I will definitely hammer their integrity without pulling any punches, shall my players see Jason Voorhes hairier brother tear apart a little girl in garou form, they will definitely suffer a breaking point with a -5 modifier, I want to be the evil storyteller\ud83d\ude08.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T01:18:07-07:00","id":1465370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465264#post1465264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your faith in us is admirable but we're human. We thought it was clear - that often happens when you understand what you're trying to say and don't see that others may not get it. Hindsight is 20/20, as they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not on topic for the thread but when it's brought up by a writer I feel I need to address this.<br /> <br /> CofD games are some of the best RPGs me and my group has played, which is why we play them much more than other RPGs, and I think it's because of terrific writers who are passionate about these games. Maybe it's because we play them so frequently (we currently play VtR, DtR, and CtL in parallell, and are about to start WtF, in addition to three non-CofD games, depending on who's available in the group and who's up to STing for that day) but it seems to me that ambiguities of that type (and similar human errors such as what appears to be omissions, or rules based on previous misremembered rules) are by far more common in CofD-games than in other games from other publishers.<br /> I don't think writers for CofD games makes such mistakes in any greater quantity than writers for other games and companies, but I absolutely believe there's a difference in the developing process in other companies that makes them catch such errors at a much higher rate.<br /> <br /> I've been vocal about this in other threads (when it's been topical) but it's my hope that a writer who has already brought up the idea that everyone makes mistakes is receptive of this criticism and possibly/hopefully bring it up to the rest of the writers or to OPP. I think that's the best I could do and hope for as a fan since the next step would be to accost the writers or the company completely unbidden, and that's quite possibly harassment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T18:50:33-07:00","id":1465456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465370#post1465370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not on topic for the thread but when it's brought up by a writer I feel I need to address this.<br /> <br /> CofD games are some of the best RPGs me and my group has played, which is why we play them much more than other RPGs, and I think it's because of terrific writers who are passionate about these games. Maybe it's because we play them so frequently (we currently play VtR, DtR, and CtL in parallell, and are about to start WtF, in addition to three non-CofD games, depending on who's available in the group and who's up to STing for that day) but it seems to me that ambiguities of that type (and similar human errors such as what appears to be omissions, or rules based on previous misremembered rules) are by far more common in CofD-games than in other games from other publishers.<br /> I don't think writers for CofD games makes such mistakes in any greater quantity than writers for other games and companies, but I absolutely believe there's a difference in the developing process in other companies that makes them catch such errors at a much higher rate.<br /> <br /> I've been vocal about this in other threads (when it's been topical) but it's my hope that a writer who has already brought up the idea that everyone makes mistakes is receptive of this criticism and possibly/hopefully bring it up to the rest of the writers or to OPP. I think that's the best I could do and hope for as a fan since the next step would be to accost the writers or the company completely unbidden, and that's quite possibly harassment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the problem CoD is the same as with WoD, a huge universe with multiple splats and variations with a multitude of different powers and weaknesses, all things you have got to account for when writing new content, this would definitely lead to an higher amount of errors and inconsistencies (just check the oWoD, it a mess there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:46:49-07:00","id":1465470,"title":"","content":"It is more complicated than that. Depends on editorial oversight, how much parallel work is done, reuse of text, schedules of every stage of the job, etc.<br /> <br /> Given the size of OPP and the amount of work being simultaneously done, I'm not surprised. Not exactly elated, but not surprised. It isn't the writers fault, precisely, as management is key here. But this is no easy feat, much less cheap.<br /> <br /> cWoD was much worse. It is easy to ignore when you had years to get used to each book and rule, but it was way worse. 1st and 2nd edition stuff were veritable nightmares on organization, clarity and consistency, hugely due to a period in which the authors followed a design theory (outdated, thank goodness) that deemed it all irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Revised was far better, but couldn't handle properly the legacy of inconsistent material. 20th An fared better, but still have a lot of problems due to legacy and simply being a huge endeavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T22:23:36-07:00","id":1465739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465252#post1465252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me expand on this further. The character isn\u2019t (shouldn\u2019t be) unconscious when they choose to spend Essence. Spending Essence on regeneration is reflexive, which can be done at any time. With injury, if the track fills with bashing you roll Stamina to remain conscious. Nothing requires the character to wait until the outcome of that roll to overcharge their regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a subtle point. I think in all my games I had assumed that characters with a full track of lethal just keel over and start bleeeding out, but based on this it seems the stamina roll to stay conscious still applies?<br /> <br /> On a slightly different note it's always bothered me that there isn't a Kuruth trigger for mortal peril. I think in my next Werewolf game I'll put forward the argument that taking agg damage should be a general Kuruth trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T02:35:50-07:00","id":1465744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465739#post1465739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a subtle point. I think in all my games I had assumed that characters with a full track of lethal just keel over and start bleeeding out, but based on this it seems the stamina roll to stay conscious still applies?<br /> <br /> On a slightly different note it's always bothered me that there isn't a Kuruth trigger for mortal peril. I think in my next Werewolf game I'll put forward the argument that taking agg damage should be a general Kuruth trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the damage is done with silver you already risk kuruth and there is a trigger for taking damage in one of the leftmost boxes but I'm not sure how convenient that would be, despite what most players seem to think, kuruth is not a good thing and shouldn't be treated as some sort of hulk mode.<br /> Now that I think of it, the fact that werewolves can regenerate without rolling for unconsciousness would mean that they can't be knocked out either unless they runned out of essence right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:10:01-07:00","id":1465760,"title":"","content":"I was looking at the various pieces of equipment in the books and the bear trap in particular, the way it works is that, when triggered, the unfortunate victim takes 3 lethal damage and is pinned in place, now, what I was thinking is how would it work for regeneration? if an uratha is stuck in a bear trap changing forms wouldn't help because it would just clamp harder and you would need opposable thumbs to roll and free yourself anyway. Now, if an uratha in garou form is stuck into such a trap how would regeneration work? the metal teeths of the trap would still be digging into the wound thus making regenaration difficult or outright impossible until succeding at a strength plus stamina roll (not that difficult in garou form) am I right here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:51:31-07:00","id":1465763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465744#post1465744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is a trigger for taking damage in one of the leftmost boxes</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there? I\u2019m not seeing it on page 103.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465744#post1465744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think of it, the fact that werewolves can regenerate without rolling for unconsciousness would mean that they can't be knocked out either unless they runned out of essence right?</div> </div> </div> </div>If their track was filled with lethal and they chose not to spend the essence to regenerate is the only way I can think of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T07:04:14-07:00","id":1465765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465763#post1465763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there? I\u2019m not seeing it on page 103.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If their track was filled with lethal and they chose not to spend the essence to regenerate is the only way I can think of</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure where I read it but I remember seing a set of triggers that activate whey you suffer damage, not sure if it was a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:15:16-07:00","id":1465771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465760#post1465760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking at the various pieces of equipment in the books and the bear trap in particular, the way it works is that, when triggered, the unfortunate victim takes 3 lethal damage and is pinned in place, now, what I was thinking is how would it work for regeneration? if an uratha is stuck in a bear trap changing forms wouldn't help because it would just clamp harder and you would need opposable thumbs to roll and free yourself anyway. Now, if an uratha in garou form is stuck into such a trap how would regeneration work? the metal teeths of the trap would still be digging into the wound thus making regenaration difficult or outright impossible until succeding at a strength plus stamina roll (not that difficult in garou form) am I right here?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can regenerate a wound without removing what's inside it. In fact, it is important to remove blades, shrapnel and the like from wounds precisely because of that. Regeneration doesn't necessarily mean all the tissue going back to place (although it preferably goes) as much as it means stopping blood loss and closing the wound as possible.<br /> <br /> I'd say with a bear trap the Uratha would regenerate as normal, but be stuck in the trap because of it. It probably means just they stay pinned, but may need to retake the damage to remove it. If the damage applied a Tilt, this should also stay while trapped as the trap prevents specific tissue from reforming properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:20:04-07:00","id":1465772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465771#post1465771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can regenerate a wound without removing what's inside it. In fact, it is important to remove blades, shrapnel and the like from wounds precisely because of that. Regeneration doesn't necessarily mean all the tissue going back to place (although it preferably goes) as much as it means stopping blood loss and closing the wound as possible.<br /> <br /> I'd say with a bear trap the Uratha would regenerate as normal, but be stuck in the trap because of it. It probably means just they stay pinned, but may need to retake the damage to remove it. If the damage applied a Tilt, this should also stay while trapped as the trap prevents specific tissue from reforming properly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see, the beartrap would still pin them in place so thats still useful, one thing I didn't read on the books is wether an immobilized target could apply its defense to attacks, the idea being that a werewolf is pinned he won't be able to dodge or apply its defense to ranged attacks and this would made sense given the fact that it can't move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:47:11-07:00","id":1465779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465251#post1465251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf regeneration isn\u2019t pretty, either. Blow the back of a Uratha\u2019s head off with a shotgun and it\u2019ll fall to the ground. Then, when its Essence healing kicks in, tendrils of blood and brain will reach out to each other. Disgusting slurping sounds happen. The gore pulls fragments of skull back together and then drags them back to what\u2019s left of the head. Weird grinding sounds occur as jagged bone bits adjust themselves like a self-assembling jigsaw, trying to work out how they fit back together. And when most of it\u2019s done, flesh and bone start growing into the gaps, leaving some splatter on the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>God damn, this is evocative. I love it.<br /> <br /> On topic, a quick skim of the books surfaces this info on reflexive actions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A reflexive action is the sort of thing you don\u2019t even need to think about doing. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An instinctual task that takes no appreciable time, such as reacting to surprise or noticing something out of the corner of your eye. </div> </div> </div>An example of a reflection action I've heard before is 'breathing', but I can't find a quote for that in the books at the moment. Either way, though - I'd allow the reflexive shift into Gauru or Essence spend on regeneration even while the character was bleeding out, conscious or otherwise, and I believe that's supported by RAW. If you don't have to 'think' about doing it, then you don't have to make a conscious choice, and people's bodies act on subconscious instinct without conscious thought all of the time. Certainly one of those instincts for Uratha is going to be &quot;heal this so I don't die.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T10:54:32-07:00","id":1465789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465771#post1465771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can regenerate a wound without removing what's inside it. In fact, it is important to remove blades, shrapnel and the like from wounds precisely because of that. Regeneration doesn't necessarily mean all the tissue going back to place (although it preferably goes) as much as it means stopping blood loss and closing the wound as possible.<br /> <br /> I'd say with a bear trap the Uratha would regenerate as normal, but be stuck in the trap because of it. It probably means just they stay pinned, but may need to retake the damage to remove it. If the damage applied a Tilt, this should also stay while trapped as the trap prevents specific tissue from reforming properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if this is how it works for Uratha though. If Uratha heal injuries without removing what's inside then a logical consequence is that many Werewolves would end up with bullets lodged in their bodies (potentially a lot of bullets), and silver buckshot to a Pure would always eventually be fatal if they couldn't get it out.<br /> <br /> Based on this, my instinct is to say that a Werewolf's body must reject foreign objects, although I could certainly see a case where after a battle wounds split and reopen as the Uratha's body forces out bullets that were sealed inside moments ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:07:38-07:00","id":1465793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465789#post1465789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if this is how it works for Uratha though. If Uratha heal injuries without removing what's inside then a logical consequence is that many Werewolves would end up with bullets lodged in their bodies (potentially a lot of bullets), and silver buckshot to a Pure would always eventually be fatal if they couldn't get it out.<br /> <br /> Based on this, my instinct is to say that a Werewolf's body must reject foreign objects, although I could certainly see a case where after a battle wounds split and reopen as the Uratha's body forces out bullets that were sealed inside moments ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The bear trap would be an expedient and nothing else, an uratha could easily pass the strength+costitution check to free itself in garou form, the important thing is that they are pinned and unable to defend themselves, that would be a lifesaver for someone trying to evade them or kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:38:05-07:00","id":1465795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465793#post1465793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The bear trap would be an expedient and nothing else, an uratha could easily pass the strength+costitution check to free itself in garou form, the important thing is that they are pinned and unable to defend themselves, that would be a lifesaver for someone trying to evade them or kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't rely on it too much. An Uratha with Unchained isn't even going to be slowed by a bear trap, and you also have to hide it, which is going to be extra difficult due to the Uratha's enhanced senses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:48:56-07:00","id":1465797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465795#post1465795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't rely on it too much. An Uratha with Unchained isn't even going to be slowed by a bear trap, and you also have to hide it, which is going to be extra difficult due to the Uratha's enhanced senses</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yes but as it has been written in the other posts, I'm trying to make a campaign where humans go against a werewolf, I made it using normal character creation so it wouldn't have any other gift aside from his starting ones, gotta give my players a chance afterall. Regarding the Uratha's senses, I think that there would be ways around it like a scent killer spray, I read about it in either the corebook or the armory supplement and it gives a -2 to any roll that uses smell to track, this and the fact that Uratha's don't keep their enhanced senses active 24/7 and you could have a reasonable chance to trigger the trap which would be nothing more than a way to buy time and get away frome the uratha (unless my players manage to figure the werewolf weakness to silver but its not going to be easy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:53:01-07:00","id":1465798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465779#post1465779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An example of a reflection action I've heard before is 'breathing', but I can't find a quote for that in the books at the moment. Either way, though - I'd allow the reflexive shift into Gauru or Essence spend on regeneration even while the character was bleeding out, conscious or otherwise, and I believe that's supported by RAW. If you don't have to 'think' about doing it, then you don't have to make a conscious choice, and people's bodies act on subconscious instinct without conscious thought all of the time. Certainly one of those instincts for Uratha is going to be &quot;heal this so I don't die.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> is one of the authors and he already stated that Essence expenditure can't be decided upon once unconscious, but can be in the very last conscious thought (between taking damage and rolling for consciousness).<br /> <br /> So we have <i>Word of God</i> on the matter. Is it the same as RAW? No, but helps to define RAI at least. And I personally find this quite a stretch of interpretation. Not every Reflexive Action is reflexive in the sense of not using conscious thought, <b>especially if it involves a decision</b>. And I can't equate the decision of breathing to the decision of expending Essence.<br /> <br /> Point being, at the moment the player may decide to spend it, but if the player decide not to for absolutely any reason, there is no point in letting the character choose freely a later moment to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465789#post1465789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this is how it works for Uratha though. If Uratha heal injuries without removing what's inside then a logical consequence is that many Werewolves would end up with bullets lodged in their bodies (potentially a lot of bullets), and silver buckshot to a Pure would always eventually be fatal if they couldn't get it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also covered by actual regeneration, the body have means to either eject or isolate foreign objects over time. Many people do live with foreign objects that got in through a wound that closed since then.<br /> <br /> But I was talking about the specific situation presented. Unless you declare that the insides of a Uratha have metal-corroding acids and whatnot, the fact is that the presence of the bear-trap can't be ignored for the moment. So the wound will close around it and the rest is semantic.<br /> <br /> Either way the Health levels will be recovered as normal, no matter what course the body takes for it, and either way you'll have to take the damage again to get free of any Tilt/Condition so the body may recover properly without a biting metal mouth.<br /> <br /> It bears to say that those traps don't actually work through the wound, though, but just by firmly grasping the leg. If no Tilt was inflicted the pin is the only consequence and the damage may otherwise just heal without further ado.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465793#post1465793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pinned and unable to defend themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure in the second part, I would have to look at the rules.<br /> <br /> But being unable to move around and being unable to defend yourself are two very different things, especially for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> A bear trap &quot;pins&quot; you in the sense that you can't <i>move away</i> from it without getting rid of it somehow. But otherwise you have some reasonable freedom of movement in place. Without RAW saying otherwise I wouldn't give more than a -1 penalty to Defense if that, to anyone in the trap, at least anyone two-legged. Four-legged animals I may be less forgiving, <i>maybe</i>.<br /> <br /> The trap is also made to be opened by a person, so it isn't exactly stellar against opponents with opposed thumbs, especially if they know what a bear trap is. One or two actions dedicated to it are enough for the Uratha to get rid of the thing.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying it isn't a valid tool. It definitely is. But it must be taken at its actual value. It slows people, don't make them defenseless, and will be even less reliable against werewolves. It is meant for animals for a reason, and it is not a humane reason. You can still take 1 or 2 turns out of one werewolf now and then if you hide it really well and hide its scent just as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:04:14-07:00","id":1465799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465797#post1465797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(unless my players manage to figure the werewolf weakness to silver but its not going to be easy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be hard to figure the weakness of a werewolf?<br /> <br /> The setting isn't built upon the supposition that werewolves never made it to pop culture, that's part of what makes their weakness a big thing.<br /> <br /> Silver is obvious, what isn't as obvious is how to get it. You can't simply go to a guns shop and ask silver bullets, that's not a thing. Silver is terrible for making weapons and takes a lot of specialized techniques to do so, because of its differences from true weapon-grade metals.<br /> <br /> I suggest you take a look at threads about silver in the Apocalypse subforum, it is a very interesting discussion, but the gist of it is that if your players don't put a lot of effort to it there will be no silver bullets, much less a silver bear trap. Just a bunch of jewels and silverware that will cost a lot more than cause damage.<br /> <br /> Oh, one last thing about the bear trap: <b>metal don't smell</b>. Metallic scent is actually due to a surface reaction between a metal and our natural oil, but a clean metal have no scent. I'd say that a Science roll with an appropriate penalty/amount of successes would let a character figure out that you can hugely reduce the trap's smell if you clean it thoroughly and then manipulate with clean gloves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:15:05-07:00","id":1465801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465798#post1465798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> is one of the authors and he already stated that Essence expenditure can't be decided upon once unconscious, but can be in the very last conscious thought (between taking damage and rolling for consciousness).<br /> <br /> So we have <i>Word of God</i> on the matter. Is it the same as RAW? No, but helps to define RAI at least. And I personally find this quite a stretch of interpretation. Not every Reflexive Action is reflexive in the sense of not using conscious thought, <b>especially if it involves a decision</b>. And I can't equate the decision of breathing to the decision of expending Essence.<br /> <br /> Point being, at the moment the player may decide to spend it, but if the player decide not to for absolutely any reason, there is no point in letting the character choose freely a later moment to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is also covered by actual regeneration, the body have means to either eject or isolate foreign objects over time. Many people do live with foreign objects that got in through a wound that closed since then.<br /> <br /> But I was talking about the specific situation presented. Unless you declare that the insides of a Uratha have metal-corroding acids and whatnot, the fact is that the presence of the bear-trap can't be ignored for the moment. So the wound will close around it and the rest is semantic.<br /> <br /> Either way the Health levels will be recovered as normal, no matter what course the body takes for it, and either way you'll have to take the damage again to get free of any Tilt/Condition so the body may recover properly without a biting metal mouth.<br /> <br /> It bears to say that those traps don't actually work through the wound, though, but just by firmly grasping the leg. If no Tilt was inflicted the pin is the only consequence and the damage may otherwise just heal without further ado.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not so sure in the second part, I would have to look at the rules.<br /> <br /> But being unable to move around and being unable to defend yourself are two very different things, especially for an Uratha.<br /> <br /> A bear trap &quot;pins&quot; you in the sense that you can't <i>move away</i> from it without getting rid of it somehow. But otherwise you have some reasonable freedom of movement in place. Without RAW saying otherwise I wouldn't give more than a -1 penalty to Defense if that, to anyone in the trap, at least anyone two-legged. Four-legged animals I may be less forgiving, <i>maybe</i>.<br /> <br /> The trap is also made to be opened by a person, so it isn't exactly stellar against opponents with opposed thumbs, especially if they know what a bear trap is. One or two actions dedicated to it are enough for the Uratha to get rid of the thing.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying it isn't a valid tool. It definitely is. But it must be taken at its actual value. It slows people, don't make them defenseless, and will be even less reliable against werewolves. It is meant for animals for a reason, and it is not a humane reason. You can still take 1 or 2 turns out of one werewolf now and then if you hide it really well and hide its scent just as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I wrote about being unable to defend themselves I was thinking more about ranged weapons, of course a werewolf could rip you apart while pinned by a trap but honestly, short of an uratha going full on matrix and dodge the bullets while standing still (although that would be funny as hell) I really can't think of any logical way they could defend against ranged weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:26:36-07:00","id":1465804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465799#post1465799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it be hard to figure the weakness of a werewolf?<br /> <br /> The setting isn't built upon the supposition that werewolves never made it to pop culture, that's part of what makes their weakness a big thing.<br /> <br /> Silver is obvious, what isn't as obvious is how to get it. You can't simply go to a guns shop and ask silver bullets, that's not a thing. Silver is terrible for making weapons and takes a lot of specialized techniques to do so, because of its differences from true weapon-grade metals.<br /> <br /> I suggest you take a look at threads about silver in the Apocalypse subforum, it is a very interesting discussion, but the gist of it is that if your players don't put a lot of effort to it there will be no silver bullets, much less a silver bear trap. Just a bunch of jewels and silverware that will cost a lot more than cause damage.<br /> <br /> Oh, one last thing about the bear trap: <b>metal don't smell</b>. Metallic scent is actually due to a surface reaction between a metal and our natural oil, but a clean metal have no scent. I'd say that a Science roll with an appropriate penalty/amount of successes would let a character figure out that you can hugely reduce the trap's smell if you clean it thoroughly and then manipulate with clean gloves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not going to make it obvious that the serial killer is a werewolf they are going to have to figure it themself and when they do, popular knowledge about silver doesn't cover the fact that it has to be 80% pure, this might look like an insignificant detail but it isn't because without having enough occult knowledge, you would risk using some cheap silverware with barely any silver in them. Regarding weapons, while its true that silver knives and such aren't easy to make, bullets are another matter entirely since you wouldn't need to make a silver bullet, just plate it with pure enough silver, silver plated weapons work only for a single attack (its written on the manual) so not a problem for a bullet, there are actual companies that sells silver bullets like Coonan.<br /> Regading bear traps, I really didn't knew about the lack of scent, thanks for the info.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:48:22-07:00","id":1465809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465801#post1465801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I wrote about being unable to defend themselves I was thinking more about ranged weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any form that lets you use Defense against firearms is basically letting you go full Matrix regardless. Unless the gunner aims specifically to the bound leg, you're overestimating how much a bear trap actually binds the victim.<br /> <br /> Plating a bullet is more complicated than that, otherwise it may not be able to be fired, or the firing may chip away the plating. For companies that sell silver bullets, take a look at prices and quality, remember that it must be at least 80% pure silver.<br /> <br /> Those aren't notions to back you from giving them any particular edge, just thought food. There's a lot of ways to handle the silver weakness depending on your decisions about the quality of the silver. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou\">Take a look at this thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:15:19-07:00","id":1465816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465809#post1465809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any form that lets you use Defense against firearms is basically letting you go full Matrix regardless. Unless the gunner aims specifically to the bound leg, you're overestimating how much a bear trap actually binds the victim.<br /> <br /> Plating a bullet is more complicated than that, otherwise it may not be able to be fired, or the firing may chip away the plating. For companies that sell silver bullets, take a look at prices and quality, remember that it must be at least 80% pure silver.<br /> <br /> Those aren't notions to back you from giving them any particular edge, just thought food. There's a lot of ways to handle the silver weakness depending on your decisions about the quality of the silver. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463875-questions-about-weapons-made-partially-of-silver-and-garou\">Take a look at this thread</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the thread link, I will have to look at an immobilized tilt but I can't seem to find any, I don't know much about silver plating but I saw a guy plating a bullet with gold and it wasn't that much difficult to be honest, we also shoot it at some ballistic gel and some of the plating was lost inside the gel, which would actually we worse for a werewolf so if you know what you are doing it can definitely be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:26:46-07:00","id":1465818,"title":"","content":"Gold have more similarities to lead than silver does in this regard, but I guess a live test is always a good option. How hard was it to plate, though? What it took? This will define time, cost and effort, and if it is viable or not to the group's necessities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:41:04-07:00","id":1465821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465818#post1465818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gold have more similarities to lead than silver does in this regard, but I guess a live test is always a good option. How hard was it to plate, though? What it took? This will define time, cost and effort, and if it is viable or not to the group's necessities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Granted I didn't follow all the process nor do I understand the science behind it but getting the material was definitely the harder (and most expensive) part, gold is not cheap so he smelted some small golden trinkets he had (he is a jeweler), he said that actually plating the bullet was the easy part, now, I don't know what the process is called or even how it works but he basically made a solution out of the gold and applied it to the bullet, when I asked if it was difficult he said that any jeweler worth his salt would be able to do it, I didn't investigate the on what kind of machinery would be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:48:38-07:00","id":1465823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465818#post1465818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gold have more similarities to lead than silver does in this regard, but I guess a live test is always a good option. How hard was it to plate, though? What it took? This will define time, cost and effort, and if it is viable or not to the group's necessities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also note that this was an handgun bullet, if you were to reload some shotgun shells it would definitely be easier, those things take anything that fit, hell, my uncle once loaded a couple with glue and they worked just fine, you would just need to find a source of silver pure enough and possibly smelt it to create some pellets but that wouldn't be necessary, jewels small enough to fit (small earings and rings, cufflinks etc.) would work just fine, of course don't expect great ballistic efficency but with a shotgun you wouldn't go farther than 50 meters anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:00:57-07:00","id":1465826,"title":"","content":"The machinery for plating isn't especially uncommon, but is specific, and yes, it is a basic process for jewelers. The problem is making it in scale for ammo. IIRC silver is about a tenth of gold's price, which is still a heft price.<br /> <br /> You also have to consider the basic fact: <i>he is a jeweler</i>. Getting the material is the hard part for <i>him</i> because everything else is already <i>his</i> business. If one of your PCs is a jeweler, then it will be far easier for them to get plated bullets.<br /> <br /> What if they're not? You may have to consider them first pursuing avenues that wouldn't work. <i>Most movies show characters casting silver bullets as they cast lead ones</i>. <u>That</u> doesn't work. So a bullet-maker that never went after learning the proper process may have a harder time than they think.<br /> <br /> A company that sells silver bullets already have all the process in place, no matter how specific this process is, as a jeweler have the process to plate small <i>objects, in small quantities</i>. But how much can those offer in a reasonable time span? At which price? What happens if you place an order too bigger than their usual one?<br /> <br /> Now, those questions have two purposes in the end: color your description of the process, and help you define how hard it is to overcome the weakness, adjusting it to your purposes. As a rule of thumb, the harder it is to get a workable silver bullet, the more it is significant for the story. It is a way to adjust the Uratha's toughness in lore without changing actual mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:29:51-07:00","id":1465830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465826#post1465826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The machinery for plating isn't especially uncommon, but is specific, and yes, it is a basic process for jewelers. The problem is making it in scale for ammo. IIRC silver is about a tenth of gold's price, which is still a heft price.<br /> <br /> You also have to consider the basic fact: <i>he is a jeweler</i>. Getting the material is the hard part for <i>him</i> because everything else is already <i>his</i> business. If one of your PCs is a jeweler, then it will be far easier for them to get plated bullets.<br /> <br /> What if they're not? You may have to consider them first pursuing avenues that wouldn't work. <i>Most movies show characters casting silver bullets as they cast lead ones</i>. <u>That</u> doesn't work. So a bullet-maker that never went after learning the proper process may have a harder time than they think.<br /> <br /> A company that sells silver bullets already have all the process in place, no matter how specific this process is, as a jeweler have the process to plate small <i>objects, in small quantities</i>. But how much can those offer in a reasonable time span? At which price? What happens if you place an order too bigger than their usual one?<br /> <br /> Now, those questions have two purposes in the end: color your description of the process, and help you define how hard it is to overcome the weakness, adjusting it to your purposes. As a rule of thumb, the harder it is to get a workable silver bullet, the more it is significant for the story. It is a way to adjust the Uratha's toughness in lore without changing actual mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are many videos about casting actual silver bullets with shooting tests, I just watched them and its almost trivial to be honest, you would need a smelter and a mold for the bullets (stuff you don't even have to make, you could just buy it from your local gun shop), anyone with a bit of experience in reloading ammo could make it. In game terms I would make it a two steps process, first they would have to cast the bullets (standard wits+craft roll) then they would have to reload them (wits+firearms roll), the equipment needed (silver included) would be equivalent to 3 dots of resources. As I wrote before, getting silver bullets should be the easy part, the difficult one would be first identifying the werewolf which is not a given since the uratha in question is an irraka and very good at stealth and also able to mess with electronics, so they are not going to have photos or videos, when they will have meet him in person (which, even with a nerfed delirium check, is still not a given) they would still have to research about it, maybe looking for a local expert that could point them toward a local uratha pack. If one of my players wanted to just trust pop culture and attack it with silver (again, nobody that doesn't have pass an occult check will be aware of the 80% pure silver limitation) in any way, it would learn its lesson the hard way (although I wouldn't kill them just like that, they are still gonna get hurt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:16:20-07:00","id":1465848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465830#post1465830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many videos about casting actual silver bullets with shooting tests, I just watched them and its almost trivial to be honest, you would need a smelter and a mold for the bullets (stuff you don't even have to make, you could just buy it from your local gun shop), anyone with a bit of experience in reloading ammo could make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I call their bullshit. Either it isn't pure enough silver or something in the video is fake.<br /> <br /> Silver melts at almost three times the melting point of lead. A common aluminum mold for bullets is two times the melting point of lead, so it'll start to deform in the instant you pour the silver.<br /> <br /> Cast iron is the other common material for casting lead bullets and don't work well, either, you need steel treated with a layer of carbon to prevent oxidation. By the way, oxidation is a huge problem through the entire process, as melted silver absorbs oxygen as a sponge does water.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">You can take a look at this blog of a writer learning how the character in a book could cast silver bullets at home</a>. If you pay attention to the many projects on casting silver bullets, what they have in common is the time and effort <i>before</i> the nice bullets could be presented, and even then there is the question of purity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:59:37-07:00","id":1465852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465848#post1465848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I call their bullshit. Either it isn't pure enough silver or something in the video is fake.<br /> <br /> Silver melts at almost three times the melting point of lead. A common aluminum mold for bullets is two times the melting point of lead, so it'll start to deform in the instant you pour the silver.<br /> <br /> Cast iron is the other common material for casting lead bullets and don't work well, either, you need steel treated with a layer of carbon to prevent oxidation. By the way, oxidation is a huge problem through the entire process, as melted silver absorbs oxygen as a sponge does water.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">You can take a look at this blog of a writer learning how the character in a book could cast silver bullets at home</a>. If you pay attention to the many projects on casting silver bullets, what they have in common is the time and effort <i>before</i> the nice bullets could be presented, and even then there is the question of purity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will have to ask my jeweler friend about smelting silver but the shotgun is obviously the better solution and an easy one at that (its even mentioned in the article), regarding the purity of silver I've been researching a little and found that dollar quarters are made out of 90% silver and the ones that are deemed &quot;junk silver&quot; (with no numismatic value) are still 90% silver and they are not rare, I've found a bundle on ebay for 50 euros, granted I don't know if they are real but since the coins are collected solely for their silver content, I'm pretty sure that they could easily sourced in most places in the U.S. regarding ballistics, I've shot coins out of shotguns and they are just as lethal as normal bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 10-29-2021, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T18:16:06-07:00","id":1465859,"title":"","content":"You can shoot anything from a shotgun, at least in theory. You're only limited to a shotgun, which is a blessing and a curse.<br /> <br /> Pure enough silver isn't hard to find, I'm saying they're not being completely honest in the videos if they're saying it is pure enough silver AND using regular bullet casting.<br /> <br /> They may be either using an alloy, an actual fake, or simply be using more specific equipment and methods than they're being forward about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T22:56:36-07:00","id":1465870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465147-death-while-in-hishu-form?p=1465798#post1465798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> is one of the authors</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm well aware. That's why I said that I believe my personal ruling is supported by RAW instead of claiming it's RAI - exactly because we're lucky enough to have the writers and devs around the forums and Discord, making speculating on RAI unnecessary in so many cases. But some tables have a higher population of death-of-the-author types, and having played in those tables in the past, being able to draw a clean line from a conclusion to existing systems definitions and terminology can help.<br /> <br /> I only quoted Bunyip there because of how amazing I found the description of regeneration to be - the rest of my post was directed at the general topic of the thread. That said, the post I quoted does <i>also</i> directly say that Essence can be spent while unconscious for reflexive things like healing, so it does seem to be RAI as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 10-30-2021, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}